detRep -- compute determinantal representations
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        detRep f
        detRep(f, Tolerance => 1e-6)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial with
        real coefficients
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note HyperbolicPt: Determinantal representations of hyperbolic plane
        cubics, => ..., default value null,
      * *note Software: Determinantal representations of bivariate polynomials,
        => ..., default value M2engine,
      * Tolerance => ..., default value .000001
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of matrices, each giving a
        determinantal representation of $f$

Description
===========

This method is a wrapper function for the various methods implemented in this
package. Currently it accepts quadrics (in any number of variables), bivariate
polynomials or homogeneous trivariate polynomials, and cubic polynomials in 4
variables. By default, all polynomials are assumed to have real coefficients.
For any polynomial falling in one of these categories, the user may call this
method, and the correct algorithm will be automatically applied. For details on
each case, see the pages below.

See also
========

  * *note Determinantal representations of quadrics: Determinantal
    representations of quadrics,
  * *note Determinantal representations of bivariate polynomials: Determinantal
    representations of bivariate polynomials,
  * *note Determinantal representations of hyperbolic plane cubics:
    Determinantal representations of hyperbolic plane cubics,

Ways to use detRep:
===================

  * "detRep(RingElement)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note detRep: detRep, is a *note method function with options:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

