randomUnipotent -- constructs a random unipotent matrix
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        randomUnipotent n
        randomUnipotent(n, R)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, or *note RR: (Macaulay2Doc)RR, or
        *note CC: (Macaulay2Doc)CC, (of type *note InexactFieldFamily:
        (Macaulay2Doc)InexactFieldFamily,)
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a random $n\times n$ unipotent
        matrix, over the ring $R$

Description
===========

This method returns a random unipotent matrix of a given size $n$, which is
upper triangular with all diagonal entries equal to $1$. if a ring $R$ is
provided, then the output is a matrix over $R$ - by default, the output is a
matrix over *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,.



+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : randomUnipotent 5                         |
|                                               |
|o1 = | 1 9/2 9/4 3/4  7/4  |                   |
|     | 0 1   7/9 7/10 7/10 |                   |
|     | 0 0   1   7/3  7    |                   |
|     | 0 0   0   1    3/7  |                   |
|     | 0 0   0   0    1    |                   |
|                                               |
|              5       5                        |
|o1 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : randomUnipotent(3, CC)                    |
|                                               |
|o2 = | 1 .424521+.641878ii .267055+.0430999ii ||
|     | 0 1                 .500492+.387244ii  ||
|     | 0 0                 1                  ||
|                                               |
|                3         3                    |
|o2 : Matrix CC    <-- CC                       |
|              53        53                     |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : randomUnipotent(3, RR[x,y])               |
|                                               |
|o3 = | 1 .98071 .65684  |                      |
|     | 0 1      .215998 |                      |
|     | 0 0      1       |                      |
|                                               |
|                        3                 3    |
|o3 : Matrix (RR  [x..y])  <-- (RR  [x..y])     |
|               53                53            |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Ways to use randomUnipotent:
============================

  * "randomUnipotent(ZZ)"
  * "randomUnipotent(ZZ,Thing)"

