roundMatrix -- lifts matrix over RR to matrix over QQ
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        roundMatrix(n, A)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, with real entries
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a threshold for rounding digits
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a matrix over QQ, obtained by
        rounding entries of A

Description
===========

This method converts a real matrix to a rational matrix, by rounding each
entry. The input $n$ specifies the number of (decimal) digits used for
rounding.



+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = matrix{{1, 2.5, -13/17}, {2*pi, 4.7, sqrt(2)}}|
|                                                       |
|o1 = | 1       2.5 -.764706 |                          |
|     | 6.28319 4.7 1.41421  |                          |
|                                                       |
|                2         3                            |
|o1 : Matrix RR    <-- RR                               |
|              53        53                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : roundMatrix(5, A)                                 |
|                                                       |
|o2 = | 1             5/2   -76471/100000 |             |
|     | 628319/100000 47/10 141421/100000 |             |
|                                                       |
|              2       3                                |
|o2 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note realPartMatrix: realPartMatrix, -- real part of a matrix over CC

Ways to use roundMatrix:
========================

  * "roundMatrix(ZZ,Matrix)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note roundMatrix: roundMatrix, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

